// The Windows executable's icon.
//
// Configured rather than committed as-is so the path can be absolute: rc.exe
// resolves a relative one against its own working directory, which is the
// build tree, and the icon is not there.
//
// Resource id 1, and it has to be the lowest in the file: Explorer shows the
// first icon in id order for the executable, and that is what a shortcut, the
// taskbar and the .zaro document icon all end up displaying.
1 ICON "@ZARO_ICON_ICO@"
